00:00:43.933 --> 00:00:49.213
So just to give you some context on the
why of choosing this system, so this

00:00:49.233 --> 00:00:54.293
system having an n8n system running
on the cloud on your own server

00:00:54.453 --> 00:00:58.473
allows you to have it first always on as
if you were to fork it on your computer,

00:00:58.613 --> 00:01:03.107
you don't pay per-run pricing and overall
this cuts about half of the costs when it

00:01:03.147 --> 00:01:08.460
comes to the cloud costs of running
these models on n8n's own cloud.

00:01:08.727 --> 00:01:13.353
You have access to the server logs which
is something that you don't get via the

00:01:13.353 --> 00:01:17.840
cloud which allows you to find problems
that you would not find otherwise.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:22.127
And of course your keys and your credentials
are more protected because they live

00:01:22.127 --> 00:01:24.407
within an instance that you fully control.

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:29.187
It's quite interesting actually because
via the server logs you can query the

00:01:29.227 --> 00:01:33.960
database directly. So you can basically
live code troubleshooting in a way that is

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:38.667
extremely dynamic and fast, which you
can't do once you're using a normal cloud

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:43.547
subscription. So this is just a system
in numbers, so you get a glimpse of it.

